SCORP SYSTEM PORTAL - MULTI-CONSOLE ARCHITECTURE AGREEMENT
==========================================================

This unified system platform, core routing architecture, multi-generation console 
selection array, and specialized utility deployment hub designed for cross-platform 
device modifications (incorporating dedicated execution logic blocks for PlayStation 3, 
PlayStation 4, and PlayStation 5 environments), is the exclusive, non-transferable 
intellectual property of Ahmed Essam (GitHub: scorpion511).

SECTION I: PLATFORM INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY & AUTHENTICITY

1. BRAND ANCHORING & ARCHITECTURAL DEPLOYMENT
   The visual framework layout, navigational design parameters, selection menu mechanics, 
   and curated directory listings known as "SCORPION HACK ALL IN 1" are uniquely compiled 
   and authored by Ahmed Essam. Any community deployment, public server mirror, or network 
   fork of this repository must preserve visible and un-altered front-end attribution strings 
   ("Designed and Compiled By Ahmed Essam") on the core presentation wrapper at all times.

2. REPACKAGING & PLAGIARISM REVENUE PENALTIES
   No external developer, entity, or competitor has the authority to remove the original 
   author's signatures, extract structural styling scripts, or place a conflicting 
   license file over unauthorized duplicates of this file package tree. Doing so voids 
   all usage tracking permissions and flags the copied repository as a pirated distribution.

3. DEVICE SUITE & ZONE DEPLOYMENTS
   This charter provides explicit layout ownership and configuration protections covering 
   the custom navigation screens for:
   - PS3 Device Selection Subsections
   - PS4 Device Selection & Multi-Firmware Exploitation Arrays
   - PS5 Device Engineering Frameworks
   - PS Tools Compilation Arrays
   - PKG-ZONE Site Custom Navigation Infrastructure
   - Custom Embedded Counter & Visual Theme Scripts

SECTION II: EXTERNAL COMPONENTS & RUNTIME CLAUSES

1. INDEPENDENT BINARY ROUTINES
   This master interface serves as a visual wrapper that initializes independent, 
